  "headline": "Indonesia Schedules Selection Of New Vice President For December",
  "seoTitle": "Indonesia to Select New Vice President in December",
  "metaDescription": "The Indonesian legislature has scheduled a plenary session for December 2, 2026, to elect a new vice president following a resignation.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The People's Consultative Assembly of Indonesia will convene a plenary session on December 2, 2026, to elect a replacement vice president.",
    "Various political parties are discussing potential candidates, with some suggesting internal party leaders or figures with established working histories.",
    "Several political factions have clarified their stances on the selection, ranging from active promotion of specific names to choosing not to nominate candidates."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Following the resignation of the vice president, the Indonesian government has moved to initiate the constitutional succession process. The People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) has officially set the date for the plenary session to appoint a successor for December 2, 2026. This selection process has triggered a series of discussions among the nation's political coalition parties. While some parties have begun suggesting potential figures for the position—including individuals with previous experience working alongside the current administration—other political entities have stated they will refrain from submitting names to respect the process managed by the incumbent coalition. The discourse involves a wide range of parties, each evaluating their position on how the new candidate should be selected and what qualifications are considered essential for the role during the remainder of the current executive term.",
